      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-110422",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n$f(x, y) = {4xy,\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1, 0 \\le y \\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\n\nThe marginal CDF $F_{X}(x)$ of $X$ is given by\n\n$F_{X}(x) = {0,\\begin{vmatrix}x < 0 \\\\ g(x),\\end{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1; 1 \\mid x > 1$.\n\nWhat is the function $g(x)$?"
    },
