      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-142925",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n$f(x, y) = {(2y)/((x + 1)^{2}),\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0, 0 \\le y \\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\n\nThe marginal CDF $F_{Y}(y)$ of $Y$ is given by\n\n$F_{Y}(y) = {0,\\begin{vmatrix}y < 0 \\\\ g(y),\\end{vmatrix}0 \\le y \\le 1; 1, \\mid y > 1$.\n\nWhat is the function $g(y)$?"
